            <ArticleTitle>Edwards Sapien 3 Valve for Mitral Replacement in a Child After Melody Valve Endocarditis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e429-e430</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(17)31090-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.08.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the surgical implantation in mitral position of the Edwards Sapien 3 valve for prosthetic valve endocarditis in a severely ill child after multiple valve replacements. The procedure was safely performed and provided adequate hemodynamic results in the short term. This report highlights the excellent potential of Sapien 3 valve for the treatment of mitral valve disease in children with a mitral valve annulus of appropriate size. Of note, the use of the Sapien 3 valve should be considered when a bioprosthesis is required at the time of valve re-replacement.</AbstractText>
